# Docket Gap Tool v0.4.2

This version fixes generic wrapper ZIP folders such as `New folder (3)`. If your downloaded documents ZIP contains subfolders inside a generic parent folder, the tool now matches against the real inner case folders instead of the outer wrapper.

# Docket Gap Tool

Start with `README_FIRST.md` for the one-click workflow.

This package inventories downloaded bankruptcy docket artifacts, parses Bloomberg docket printout PDFs or text files, applies configurable skip/keep rules, and creates an Excel workbook showing which entries are downloadable now versus request-needed.

## Fast start

1. Put downloaded case ZIPs into `input/downloaded_artifacts/`.
2. Put browser-saved docket PDFs into `input/docket_pdfs/`.
3. Run one of:
   - macOS: `RUN_ME_MAC.command`
   - Windows: `RUN_ME_WINDOWS.bat`
   - Linux: `bash RUN_ME_LINUX.sh`
4. Open `output/docket_gap_download_request_by_case.xlsx`.

## Command-line examples

Single case from PDF:

```bash
docket-gap analyze \
  --artifact-zip "input/downloaded_artifacts/Alpha Natural Resources, Inc.zip" \
  --case-folder "Penn Virginia Corp" \
  --case-name "Penn Virginia Corp" \
  --docket-pdf "input/docket_pdfs/penn_virginia.pdf" \
  --output-dir output_penn
```

Force OCR for a scanned PDF:

```bash
docket-gap import-pdf --input-pdf input/docket_pdfs/penn_virginia.pdf --ocr force
```

Folder-based one-click run from terminal:

```bash
docket-gap auto
```


Word docket files: put `.docx` files in `input/docket_word_docs/`. Do not put them in `input/docket_texts/`; that folder is only for `.txt`.


## v0.4.3 fix

This version fixes downloaded-artifact matching when your downloaded ZIP contains case ZIPs inside a generic parent folder, for example:

```text
New folder (3).zip
  New folder (3)/
    Akorn, Inc..zip
    Chinos Holdings.zip
```

The tool now opens those nested case ZIPs and inventories the PDFs inside them instead of treating `New folder (3)` as the case folder or misreading `(3)` as docket entry 3.
